# The fields of the Air and Water Database (AWDB) of the Natural Resources Conservation Service (NRCS).
# A generator wrote them, their types and src/main/resources/awdb/operations.json from the OpenAPI
# document of its REST API, one field for each read operation. The descriptions are written by hand.
# Each field is fetched by a RestOperationFetcher, see AwdbConfiguration.

extend type Query {
	# The Air and Water Database (AWDB) of the Natural Resources Conservation Service (NRCS) holds the readings
	# of automated snow stations in the western mountains (SNOTEL), snow courses, soil climate stations and
	# reservoirs, and the water supply forecasts for western rivers.

	"""
	Snow, soil, weather and streamflow stations of the Air and Water Database of the Natural Resources Conservation
	Service (NRCS), with their name, location, elevation, county and watershed, such as the automated SNOTEL snow
	stations in the Colorado mountains. stationTriplets *:CO:SNTL lists the 118 SNOTEL stations of Colorado, and
	countyNames narrows the list to a county. Without a filter the answer holds all 4,398 stations of the United
	States, about 1.6 MB.
	"""
	awdbStations(
		"""
		Station triplets, each written stationId:stateCode:networkCode, for example 335:CO:SNTL for Berthoud Summit,
		separated by commas. A part can be the wildcard *: *:CO:SNTL is every SNOTEL station in Colorado.
		"""
		stationTriplets: String
		"Station names, separated by commas, for example Berthoud Summit. A name can contain the wildcard *."
		stationNames: String
		"The codes of the data collection offices, separated by commas, for example CO."
		dcoCodes: String
		"""
		County names, separated by commas, for example Grand or Clear Creek. A name can contain the wildcard *.
		"""
		countyNames: String
		"""
		Only stations that measure one of these elements, written elementCode:heightDepth:ordinal and separated by
		commas, for example WTEQ for snow water equivalent. The height or depth and the ordinal are optional.
		"""
		elements: String
		"""
		Only stations with data of one of these durations, separated by commas, for example DAILY or HOURLY.
		"""
		durations: String
		"Hydrologic unit codes of watersheds, separated by commas. A code can contain the wildcard *."
		hucs: String
		"If true, return forecast point metadata for stations that are forecast points"
		returnForecastPointMetadata: Boolean
		"If true, return reservoir metadata for reservoir stations"
		returnReservoirMetadata: Boolean
		"If true, return the list of station elements for each station"
		returnStationElements: Boolean
		"If true, only return active stations and station elements"
		activeOnly: Boolean
	): [AwdbStation]

	"""
	How deep the snow is and how much water it holds at a mountain snow station (SNOTEL) of the NRCS, as daily,
	hourly, monthly or yearly readings for a date range: the snow depth (element SNWD), the snow water equivalent
	(WTEQ), the air temperature (TOBS) and the precipitation (PREC), for example at Berthoud Summit, station
	335:CO:SNTL, on the road over Berthoud Pass west of Denver. centralTendencyType adds the 30-year median or average of each value. By default
	each daily value carries the date at the end of its period, a day later than the AWDB SOAP service dates the
	same value; periodRef START gives the dates that SOAP gives.
	"""
	awdbData(
		"""
		Station triplets, each written stationId:stateCode:networkCode, for example 335:CO:SNTL for Berthoud Summit,
		separated by commas. A part can be the wildcard *.
		"""
		stationTriplets: String!
		"""
		The elements to read, written elementCode:heightDepth:ordinal and separated by commas, for example WTEQ,SNWD for
		snow water equivalent and snow depth, or PREC for precipitation. The height or depth and the ordinal are
		optional.
		"""
		elements: String!
		"How long each value covers. Leave it out for DAILY."
		duration: AwdbDurationName
		"""
		The first date to read, as yyyy-MM-dd, for example 2026-04-01, or a date relative to today in units of the
		duration, such as -7 for seven days ago.
		"""
		beginDate: String
		"The last date to read, as yyyy-MM-dd, for example 2026-04-07, or 0 for today."
		endDate: String
		"""
		The date from which to retrieve new or changed data. Expects either yyyy-MM-dd HH:mm or MM/dd/yyyy HH:mm format.
		Hours and minutes are optional and will be considered as 00 if not specified.
		"""
		insertOrUpdateBeginDate: String
		"""
		Whether a value carries the date at the START or at the END of the period it covers. Leave it out for END, which
		dates a daily value one day later than the AWDB SOAP service.
		"""
		periodRef: AwdbPeriodReference
		"Also return the 30-year median, the average, or both with each value."
		centralTendencyType: AwdbCentralTendency
		"If true, return the flags with each data value"
		returnFlags: Boolean
		"If true, return original values (and original flags if returnFlags=true)"
		returnOriginalValues: Boolean
		"If true, data marked as suspect will not be filtered out"
		returnSuspectData: Boolean
	): [AwdbStationData]

	"""
	How much water a river of the western United States will carry this spring and summer, as snow melts: the
	seasonal water supply forecasts of the NRCS, such as the April to July streamflow volume of the Big Thompson
	River at the canyon mouth, station 06738000:CO:USGS, in thousands of acre-feet, with a value for each exceedance
	probability and the normal for the period.
	"""
	awdbForecasts(
		"""
		Station triplets of forecast points, each written stationId:stateCode:networkCode, for example 06738000:CO:USGS
		for the Big Thompson River at the canyon mouth, separated by commas. A part can be the wildcard *.
		"""
		stationTriplets: String!
		"A comma separated list of element codes. Examples: RESC, SRVO, SRVOO, JDAY, REST"
		elementCodes: String
		"""
		The beginning of the publication date period for which to retrieve data. Expects either 'yyyy-MM-dd' or
		'MM/dd/yyyy' format. Defaulted to the start of the current water year, if not specified.
		"""
		beginPublicationDate: String
		"""
		The end of the publication date period for which to retrieve data. Expects either 'yyyy-MM-dd' or 'MM/dd/yyyy'
		format. Defaulted to current day, if not specified.
		"""
		endPublicationDate: String
		"""
		A comma separated list of exceedence probabilities. Example: "10,30,50"
		"""
		exceedenceProbabilities: String
		"""
		A comma separated list of forecast periods. Examples: 03-01,07-31 or [03-01,07-31] or [,07-31] or [03-01,]
		"""
		forecastPeriods: String
	): [AwdbForecast]

	"""
	The codes that the NRCS Air and Water Database uses, with their names and units: elements such as WTEQ (snow
	water equivalent) and SNWD (snow depth), networks such as SNTL (SNOTEL), durations, states, units, instruments
	and forecast periods. referenceLists chooses the lists; without it every list comes back.
	"""
	awdbReferenceData(
		"""
		A comma-separated list of reference data to return. Options include: dcos, durations, elements, forecastPeriods,
		functions, instruments, networks, physicalElements, states, and units. If not specified, all the lists are
		returned.
		"""
		referenceLists: String
	): AwdbReferenceData
}

"A station of the NRCS Air and Water Database, such as a SNOTEL snow station."
type AwdbStation {
	"The station triplet of the station"
	stationTriplet: String
	"The id of the station"
	stationId: String
	"The 2-character state code of the station"
	stateCode: String
	"The network code of the station"
	networkCode: String
	"The name of the station"
	name: String
	"The DCO code of the station"
	dcoCode: String
	"The name of the county that the station is located in"
	countyName: String
	"The hydrologic unit code of the station"
	huc: String
	"The elevation of the station in feet."
	elevation: Float
	"The latitude of the station"
	latitude: Float
	"The longitude of the station"
	longitude: Float
	"The timezone offset from GMT of the data for the station"
	dataTimeZone: Float
	"The NRCS pedon code for the station"
	pedonCode: String
	"The SHEF id of the station"
	shefId: String
	"The entity in charge of the station"
	operator: String
	"The date that the station was put into service"
	beginDate: String
	"The date that the station was taken out of service or 2100-01-01 if still in service"
	endDate: String
	"Contains information about a forecast point"
	forecastPoint: AwdbForecastPoint
	"Contains reservoir metadata"
	reservoirMetadata: AwdbReservoirMetadata
	"The station elements of the station"
	stationElements: [AwdbStationElement]
	"Hydrologic units within 5000m of this station"
	associatedHucs: [String]
}

"Contains information about a forecast point"
type AwdbForecastPoint {
	"The name of the forecast point"
	name: String
	"The user name of the forecaster who forecasts for this station"
	forecaster: String
	"The name to display in the UI for the profile type"
	exceedenceProbabilities: [Int]
}

"Contains reservoir metadata"
type AwdbReservoirMetadata {
	"The capacity of the reservoir in acre-feet"
	capacity: Float
	"The elevation of the reservoir (in feet) when it is at capacity"
	elevationAtCapacity: Float
	"The usable capacity of the reservoir in acre-feet"
	usableCapacity: Float
}

